WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Hello, I’m Robert Schaub.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.720
I spent 38 years in software engineering
and project leadership—

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:12.260
30 at Phonak/Sonova,
helping people hear better.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.960
I founded FactHarbor Verein,
a Swiss non-profit,

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.860
and built FactHarbor’s evidence-based
fact-checking Alpha

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:25.840
and Our AI Charter Runtime, a runnable
decision-gateway proof of concept.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:28.220
My motivation is societal:

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.840
facts are an essential foundation
of democracy and justice.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.580
I want AI systems to strengthen evidence-based
decision-making and accountability.

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:45.400
For consequential answers, that means checking
authority and evidence before release

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.720
and giving affected people a record
they can inspect and challenge.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.720
The FactHarbor Alpha assesses public claims
against supporting and opposing evidence.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.780
Here is a report from the public Alpha.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.360
It examines a blanket heat-pump recommendation
for a Winterthur home

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.080
and records supporting
and opposing evidence,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.400
sources, limitations, uncertainty
and its verdict.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:17.980
For the prototype, selected claim reports will be
prepared in advance for the decision gateway.

00:01:18.495 --> 00:01:24.260
A later product could acquire new evidence
under explicit authority and limits.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:28.260
Evidence-Gated Agents will test this path.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.700
An AI may draft a consequential answer,
but the gateway outside the model

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:40.880
decides whether current authority and declared
evidence support releasing that exact answer.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:47.520
If the gateway blocks it, the request may be
narrowed—or the person may decline.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:52.240
Any new answer must be based
on current authority and evidence

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.040
and pass every check again before release.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.980
If released, the recipient receives
an inspectable receipt

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.780
linking the answer, authority, evidence,
decision and outcome.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:11.400
Beyond the prototype, I want to develop
evidence-gated decision-making applications and services

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:16.320
for companies, public bodies,
newsrooms and civil society.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:22.560
With permission, they could weigh an organisation’s
policies, contracts and records

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.360
alongside public evidence.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.340
People affected by an answer should be able
to understand it,

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:32.380
challenge it, and seek correction
or independent review.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.960
I built both foundations
and can integrate them directly.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:42.440
The Prototype Fund’s coaches and other participants
can challenge my assumptions,

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:48.860
improve the recipient experience, and connect me
with practitioners who can test

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:54.080
whether the receipt is understandable
and whether AI is justified.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.420
My vision is a free and fair society

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:02.800
in which technology strengthens democracy
because consequential decisions

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:05.880
remain authorised, evidence-grounded

00:03:06.045 --> 00:03:07.660
and open to challenge.
